0..67 Comment "// The refusals of implicit parameters: a call omitting an implicit"
68..135 Comment "// nothing determines, one whose only solution names a binder of an"
136..213 Comment "// argument\'s own lambda, a call whose argument and expected type disagree on"
214..282 Comment "// one, an implicit written among the parentheses, a resident naming"
283..355 Comment "// no implicit, a use standing as a value with an implicit unsupplied, a"
356..431 Comment "// supply standing as a value whose implicit, once the supply abstracts the"
432..504 Comment "// explicit parameter before it, holds no value of that parameter, and a"
505..549 Comment "// telescope whose types mention each other."
550..552 Comment "//"
553..567 Comment "// - see: #315"
568..583 Comment "// - see: #1216"
